/E (Content Translation: Content for students who are already using Athena and retention. BTS content lives here: students quotes, case studies, success stories, and power-user tips on how students use Athena. All of it reads as lived experience, not brand claims. The tone feels like a coach checking in, not a company retaining a subscriber: warm, personal, a little celebratory when it's earned. Efficacy is a big lever here. It needs students to feel seen for their progress, share their tips, and give them content they want to share with friends.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [9]
>>
